@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@challengeToken =

### 2FA status (needs a session; run the login request from auth.http first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/2fa

### 1. Start setup: returns the secret (base32) and the otpauth URI. Needs TWO_FACTOR_ENCRYPTION_KEY on the server
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/2fa/setup
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

### 2. Confirm with the 6-digit code from the authenticator app: returns the recovery codes (shown once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/2fa/enable
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{ "code": "123456" }

### New recovery codes (needs the app code; the old ones stop working)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/2fa/recovery-codes
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{ "code": "123456" }

### Disable: password + (app code OR recovery code)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/2fa/disable
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{ "password": "Senha#12345", "code": "123456" }

### Login step 2 (after POST /auth/login answered twoFactorRequired): paste the challengeToken above
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/2fa/verify
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{baseUrl}}

{ "challengeToken": "{{challengeToken}}", "code": "123456" }

### Login step 2 with a recovery code
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/2fa/verify
# Content-Type: application/json
# Origin: {{baseUrl}}
#
# { "challengeToken": "{{challengeToken}}", "recoveryCode": "ABCDE-FGHIJ" }
